A||||14||JSocha||The official "Pitty Pot" thread.  Come join the sadness!||||1||
Z||000000||JSocha||06-14-2001||03:31 PM||||Come on in, this thread is dedicated for all those that need a "Pitty Pot" every now and again to P their life stories in.<P>Since I'm here at the podium, I may as well start.<P>Last year in March, bought a new Dodge 2001 one ton and only a few months after I picked it up, the tranny went out.  Got it replaced.<P>On Thursday, May 18 of 2000 at about 7:32 PM my poodle Peaches of 9 years passed away in my arms to which devistated me for many months thereafter and still to this day.<P>Nothing like stress I tell you.<P>In June of that year, went scuba diving up at the lake and because very ill with a hellish rash.<P>In July and at the request and pleading of my wife, due to experieincing chest pains, I went in for a physical to find out my cholestrol levels were very high.  Later that day, I get a call from the Doctor, "I've got good news!  You have TYPE 2 Diabities." (T2 D).  Where in the worlds is the good news there?<P>Been fighting this issue since with doctors and/or specialist's who I feel really do not know their heads from a hole in the ground.<P>In November, finally purchased a house that was only three years old to get my wife out of the house we were living in due to her alergys.<P>In December, just about loose Baby, step sister to Peaches, to heat exhaustion and dhydration as I covered their kennels in our heated garage that evening because of a blizzard and extremly low windchills where the temp in the garage was only reaching about 40.<P>March of 2001, income taxes through the roof.<P>May, take my Fiero in to have a dealership look over the vehicle and fix certain items that I knew were wrong.  Car still there, tranny I got was an Izuzu not a Muncie so now ordered the rebuilt.<P>In May, Socha curse once again takes place.  Go to buy my wife the rototiller she wanted for Mothers day, get it home, start it up...no belt!  Wait for a week for the belt.<BR>Still battling doctors on the T2 D.<P>At about the middle/end of May, a fellow resident and I who several years back got together to spar and work out together.  Him with Taekwondo, me with my style I was involved in at the time.  During the sparing, we went into it a little more and a little harder and I ended up pinning him to which I thought nothing of.  Now he wants a rematch (didn't know we were competing then), which I really don't want and to which I didn't realize how personally he had taken it.  How do I get him to just let it go?<P>Is like 32/33 a magical year in life where all the $h*t that didn't happen prior in your life just starts happeing now or what!?<P>First weekend of June, get the sprinkler system to our yard hooked up and running, only to have a major leak occur in one of the pipes.  10' x 12' x 5' hole now dug (by hand) where the leak is and now I can't get anybody to fix it.<P>Get promising news from recent doctor.<P>Over this past weekend, purchase a bike and go on an exercise program.<P>Yesterday, get bad news from doctor while going in to see why I'm feeling down.<P>Go in first thing this morning after setting up another appointment with a different doctor only to find out the lab "has" apparently screwed up on my blood work, possibly again.  Not to worry though, I am apparently a human pin cushion with an inexahastable supply of blood to be taken at any time.<P>BTW, what in the h3ll disease or virus is "Staki Batriatris"????<P>At noon, the brand new bike I had bought over the weekend which is in my garage, the Socha curse once again has taken over. I move the bike so that I can get at one of my toolbox drawers, when I here this "clink" sound.  Look down to see the peddle laying on the floor still attached to the peddle arm.  I pick it up thinking that the screw/bolt came loose and I am going to reattach it.  WRONG!  Part of the shaft that also goes to the other side and the other peddle is still attached and in the little hole to the arm that fell off   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>Now I'm just sitting here reading and responding to threads after lunch, getting caught up on the recent posts, only to have our Accountant come back only moments after me from her lunch break to ask and tell me that my front tire on the drivers side is flat and she was listening to it go "sssssstttttt" while watching it go flat.<P>Go out...yep...tire is completely flat now...raining out as well...but I go to the back of the truck to get the hydraulic jack out of my truck bed and my back passenger side, inner tire doesn't look right.  FLAT as well and partially off the rim!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>&lt;screaming&gt; AUUUUGGGGGGHHHHHHHH!  What else can go wrong in my life?!?!?!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Okay, I'm stepping down from the "pitty pot" so somebody else can have center stage.<p>[This message has been edited by JSocha (edited 06-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Steve Normington||06-14-2001||03:40 PM||||I've been F***ing around with my Fiero since September and it's still not running!<P>(Short and to the point).||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fierochic88||06-14-2001||03:42 PM||||Man that all sucks!  I don't think I can top you at all, nor shall I try!  The worst thing that happened to me recently was Tuesday I thought I was going to have to have an appendectomy, but luckily (i guess) it is just some gastro-intestinal virus.  <P>However, don't give up hope on the Diabetes!  If in fact, you do have it, there are definitely ways of dealing with it.  Both my father and grandmother (who resides with us) have it, so I deal with the issue on a daily basis.  My father is worse off than my grandmother, but has still combatted it for nearly 8 years on the pills.  She has been on the pills for 10 years quite successfully.<P>Best of luck with your tire!<P><BR>Jennifer<BR>Silver 88 GT<BR>Silver 86 Cp<BR>Cobalt Blue 86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||Galen||06-14-2001||03:47 PM||||A lil P in my life? I normally put the P in the toilet.. thats where it should be, unless I'm out in the woods.. then the nearest tree withot animals in it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> can't have animals staring at me. hehe<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/redcreature.gif">     <BR> <A HREF="mailto:galen@spinrpg.com">galen@spinrpg.com</A>  -<A HREF="http://myfiero.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>1988 Hawaiin Orchid Coupe w/ sunroof</A><BR>AIM: GalenRPG - <A HREF="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank>WebJolt Pictures</A>||||reg||1
