Z||000005||stimpy||06-14-2001||03:55 PM||||Luck is a funny thing. For example, your bike pedal could have snapped while pedalling vigoursly, resulting in racking your junk on the top bar and spraining your ankle painfully resulting in you face catapulting over the handlebars landing face first on the freshly graveled road.<BR>After several weeks with your jaw wired shut hobbling to the bathroom due to the liquid diet giving you loose stool, you are finally able to drive to the dentist to have the bridge put in to replace all the teeth shattred in the fall, when your front tire has a devestating blowout on the freeway, flipping your car and crushing several vertebrae.<P>Now, aren't you <B>glad</B> your bike pedal broke in the grage? ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Ken Wittlief||06-14-2001||04:08 PM||||Slap Slap Slap - snap out of it son.<P> find yourself a church or chapel and this Sunday go down and thank God that things are happening to you<P>that you can handle, get though, and deal with.<P>  Im sure there are plenty of people on here that are having stuff land in their laps that they dont think they can handle, dont think they will survive, and have no idea how to begin to deal with.<P>or to look at it another way: King Solomon, one of the wisest and richest men in history;<P> 1. Never had air conditioning in his home<BR> 2. Never got to drive a pickup truck<BR> 3. Never flew in an aircraft<BR> 4. Never tasted a hot fudge sunday<BR> 5. Never had a Carolina Barbeque sandwich<BR> 6. Never looked at the moon or the milky way through a pair of binoculars<BR> 7. Never had the chance to go to Hawaii, or to take his kids to Disney World<BR> 8. Never saw a Bald Eagle soar over the rocky Mountains<BR> 9. Never had a porcelin toilet<BR>10. Never knew what it was like to put on a cotton undershirt on a chilly fall morning that just came out of the dryer.<P>  whenever I get to feeling I've gotten the short end of the stick, I go spend some time helping out someone worst off than me - even in our modern civilized world, i dont have to look very far, or very hard.<P>  one day at a time guy, its 4pm already - let tomorrow worry about itself.||||reg||1
