Z||000009||MrPBody||06-14-2001||08:43 PM||||Galen --<P>The mustardy stuff?  Uh . . . I don't know.<P>- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -<P>1988 was a weird/crappy year for us -- nothing really disastrous, but strange:  my wife's dog died in February; I turned 40; bad drought in Georgia, but on Fourth of July weekend I installed a kitchen skylight so of course it rained; the System Manager at work died, and I became System Manager (mixed blessing); and on December 29, we found a bullet on the bathroom floor -- a mangled .38 slug that apparently bounced off our neighbor's chimney and came through our window.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||btoth||06-14-2001||10:06 PM||||JSocha - sorry to hear about the endless bad luck. Seems things can only get better.<P>Not that I'm in the same situation you are, but I might as well let some stuff out too...<P>1.)  Job I was supposed to have started May 19th has been "on hold".  (Supposed to be working for the local Post Office like I did last summer.)  The postmaster just told me to "be patient"... after I called him for the 5th week in a row.  If I had known this was going to happen, I could have got a job doing computer programming for the summer! Grr.<BR>2.)  I have no money due to lack of job.<BR>3.)  All of my hobbies cost money... non of which I can affored.  Like the Fiero.<BR>4.)  Most of my friends got internships or are busy all day with work and are too tired afterwards to do much.  Normally I would be too... but now I'm just bored out of my mind.<BR>5.)  My health problems (which I've had since I was born) have been worse lately... and all this nice weather gets my allergies going...<P>Basically this summer sucks so far and I can't wait to get back to school.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Mach10||06-15-2001||10:21 AM||||Well, for the TaeKwonDo guy, take the rematch, and hammer him into the mat. Remember, TKD is USELESS at close range. Get in, avoid his feet, and take it to the mats. Of note, there is a pressure point just above the elbow, just under (towards the elbow) the bulge that is the tricep. Use the blade of your arm on it, while grabbing his wrist and forcing his arm straight. Force him down, and watch him squirm. No marks, no lasting pain, just instant incapacitation  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Sorry, that's the only help my limited experience can give you. I don't know much about the other stuff. I'd be heart-broken if my little Roo-Dog died  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000012||JSocha||06-15-2001||10:53 AM||||Thanks Mach10 for the advise and support!  Well aware of pressure and pain points. My Sensai use to use me as a practice and display dummy since I have a high threshold to pain.  <P>The guy I spared with didn't appreciate his leg being pinned (1st down) where he couldn't move and/or my knee pinning his jaw (2nd down) with his elbow bent so that his wrist was folded so all I had to do was put just a little pressure on it each time he tried to squirm out to get him to resubmit again.  It was all in fun and practice, or so I thought.  Must be a black belt thing, because every one I know/knew who became a black belt suddenly goes like postal and he seems to be no exception.  And all I tried to do was inform him he was advertising his moves prior to making them through my observation of his set points to help him out so he wouldn't broadcast what he was going to do next.<P>Hey, have you ever seen the Sicharons (spelling) Martial Arts club up there in Winnipeg put on a martial arts show?  Those dudes rock not to mention fly!  If you haven't, go check them out.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Philphine||06-15-2001||11:34 AM||||hmmm...<P>well, i found out i had a kdney stone last week. passed it pretty easy though. don't know how this will recur in the future. <P>clutch went out on my '87 fiero, the one i drive (the rest are either projects or the gt i haven't picked up yet), but i'm hoping it's just my master cylinder.<P>the supervisor took a couple days off so i'm running night shift at work. i had no real desire to be a supervisor. i liked when i got into maintenance and was going for an r&d job, but i couldn't refuse an advancement (couple years of college and all my real work experience is with this company). i try to work hard but i get no enjoyment from trying to get other people to work.<P>i'm also not the most gregarious person in the world and night shift makes it worse. i've never made much of an impression on women and now being out of phase with the rest of the world i don't even meet women to be unimpressve in front of.<P>:::sniff::: see what you' started. i'm all weepy now.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Mach10||06-23-2001||08:41 PM||||LOL...<BR>My master uses me as a attack dummy too. I have stiff wrists and low pain tolerance... Maybe Hapkido isn't my best bet?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>What I do have is self-control. (I didn't scream once when he almost broke my wrist in a demonstration, nor squirm when he choked me out to near-unconciousness :rolleyes <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>It's all good... He'd always warn me about what'll happen: "This will act harshly on your wrists..." *Crick*-"Eeep."<BR>Or, When done properly, your opponent will be knocked out within 5 seconds. 2-3, usually *Swish*"Skraa---... ... ...&lt;grey out&gt;"<BR>||||reg||7
